.nf
YASMV manual                                                 goal

.ti 0
SYNOPSIS

.in 3
goal set <name> <expression>
goal list

.ti 0
DESCRIPTION

.fi
.in 3
Save a named Boolean target for bounded and shortest reachability searches.
Use check reachable -name NAME or check progress -name NAME to resolve a saved
goal explicitly. Positional operands always refer to model expressions.

Requires a loaded model. set saves a new immutable revision; reusing a name
replaces its expression in that revision. list displays the saved expressions.
Names containing spaces must be quoted. Expressions use native syntax and are
validated when used. These commands preserve the native model and trace.

.ti 0
EXAMPLES

.nf
.in 3
>> goal set duplicate DUPLICATE
>> check reachable -name duplicate -method bmc -shortest -depth 12

.ti 0
SEE ALSO

.fi
.in 3
help workspace, help check.
